---
import { patchwork, type Patchwork } from "../../data/site";

// One glyph per kind of artifact. Six identical pills said "six things"; a
// spreadsheet, a paper cuaderno and a chat thread say what KIND of mess it is,
// which is the part a director recognises as their own Friday afternoon.
const GLYPHS: Record<Patchwork, string[]> = {
  sheet: ["M4.5 3.5h15v17h-15z", "M4.5 9h15", "M4.5 14.5h15", "M11 9v11.5"],
  paper: ["M6 3.5h7.5l4.5 4.5v12H6z", "M13.5 3.5V8H18", "M9 12h6", "M9 16h4"],
  chat: ["M4 5.5h16v10.5h-9l-5 4v-4H4z", "M8 9h8", "M8 12.5h5"],
};
---

<section class="band pain fold-band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="narrow reveal">
      <h2>El cierre de periodo, sin armar nada a mano.</h2>
      <p>
        Las notas viven en el archivo de Excel de cada docente. La asistencia,
        en papel. Los encargados preguntan por WhatsApp. Y al cierre de cada
        periodo alguien en la dirección junta todo eso, hoja por hoja, para
        poder entregar notas a tiempo.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="contrast">
      <div class="side">
        <p class="side-label">Cómo se hace hoy</p>
        <ul class="scatter reveal reveal-stagger">
          {
            patchwork.map((p, i) => (
              <li style={`--i:${i}`}>
                <svg class="glyph" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                  {GLYPHS[p.kind].map((d) => (
                    <path d={d} />
                  ))}
                </svg>
                <span class="scatter-text">
                  <span class="scatter-name">{p.label}</span>
                  <span class="scatter-meta">{p.meta}</span>
                </span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- The six sources narrowing into one. The wedge is the argument: it is
           the same information, arriving from six places and leaving from one.
           Decorative, so it carries no text and is hidden from assistive tech;
           the two labels either side already say it. -->
      <div class="funnel reveal" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="wedge"></span>
        <svg class="tip" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path d="M4 12h15M13 5.5 19.5 12 13 18.5"></path>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="side">
        <p class="side-label">Cómo se hace con Simple Manage Pro</p>
        <div class="card-lead reveal one">
          <p class="one-title">Un solo sistema</p>
          <p class="one-body">
            Las mismas notas, la misma asistencia y la misma matrícula, en un
            solo lugar y actualizadas por quien las tiene de primera mano.
          </p>
          <ul class="streams">
            <li class="chip">Notas</li>
            <li class="chip">Asistencia</li>
            <li class="chip">Matrícula</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="narrow reveal">
      <p class="aside">
        Simple Manage Pro no reemplaza nada del MEP. Ordena la información que
        el colegio ya maneja por dentro.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .contrast {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: center;
    margin-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  .side-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-info-dark);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  /* ── The six sources ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .scatter {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .scatter li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.4rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-light);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius-2);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    box-shadow: var(--elev-1);
    /* Each row sits at its own small angle. The point is legibility of the
       mess, not the mess itself: they stay readable, just visibly unaligned. */
    rotate: var(--tilt, 0deg);
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(1) {
    --tilt: -1.4deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(2) {
    --tilt: 0.9deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(3) {
    --tilt: -0.6deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(4) {
    --tilt: 1.5deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(5) {
    --tilt: -1.1deg;
  }
  .scatter li:nth-child(6) {
    --tilt: 0.7deg;
  }

  /* `rotate` rather than `transform` above, so the stagger's translateY and
     this angle do not fight over the same property. */
  .glyph {
    width: 1.4rem;
    height: 1.4rem;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-info-dark);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .scatter-name {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-dark);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .scatter-meta {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-info-dark);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  /* ── The funnel ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .funnel {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    min-height: 3.5rem;
  }

  .wedge {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 30%, transparent),
      var(--color-primary-accent) 55%,
      var(--color-primary)
    );
    /* Points down on a narrow screen, where the two sides stack. */
    clip-path: polygon(6% 0, 44% 100%, 56% 100%, 94% 0);
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .tip {
    position: relative;
    width: 1.8rem;
    height: 1.8rem;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-primary);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    rotate: 90deg;
  }

  /* ── The one system ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .one {
    --accent: var(--color-primary-fill);
  }
  .one-title {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-dark);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .one-body {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }
  .streams {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .contrast {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 9.5rem 1fr;
    }
    .scatter {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
    /* Stretched to the row, not centred in it. At a fixed height the wedge was
       shorter than the stack it is supposed to be gathering, so it read as a
       triangle sitting between two columns rather than as six things
       narrowing into one. */
    .funnel {
      align-self: stretch;
      min-height: 11rem;
    }
    .wedge {
      clip-path: polygon(0 4%, 100% 40%, 100% 60%, 0 96%);
    }
    .tip {
      rotate: none;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .scatter li {
      rotate: none;
    }
  }
</style>
